From: originaxiom <originaxiom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:12:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 5, patch 2;
 built on 5c7abd72a with the ten patches of series 4, the move of the old
 front pages and the first patch of series 5 applied): A SEAT'S BRANCH IS
 FOUND BY A NAME THAT FITS ONE BRANCH, AND A HARVEST GATE THAT COULD READ NO
 BRANCH FAILS AND SAYS SO (Review 79, the second reader's row 22; main's word
 in M10; and what the seat found on the way to the failure of M10). Four
 things. ONE: the checker found a seat's branch by the last part of its name
 and, of two that fit, took the shorter without a word, so a second seat's
 branch of the same last name would have been read in place of the first. A
 name that fits more than one branch is now refused, and the branches that fit
 are named. TWO: where a seat has no pin in the ledger's table, or its pin
 does not resolve in the clone, its entry was left with neither a head nor a
 reason, and the report raised an error of a missing key in place of the
 checker's own line. The seat is now given its reason and the report prints
 it. THREE: in a clone that holds no seat's branch the checker reads none,
 finds nothing wrong among none and ends with status 0, and the gate said that
 no seat's branch is past its pin. The gate is now refused there with its
 reason, as it is on a shallow clone: that is main's word, and the stricter
 option. FOUR: a failing checker's reason stood after one line for each seat,
 and the gate's answer was cut before it; the reason now comes first. And
 where the gate read some branches and not others it passes, and its sentence
 counts those it did not read and names the first three: a gate says what it
 did not read. Where every branch is read the sentence is word for word the
 one main's own test holds. On this clone the sentence now ends: 1 seat(s) not
 read in this clone, the one whose remote is not configured here. What it does
 not reach: a branch that is in the clone and is not the seat's; a clone that
 holds an old copy of a seat's branch reads that copy. The lock: four tests
 added to tests/test_gates_are_a_function_of_the_commit.py, each on a small
 repository with a remote of its own. On the commit before, all four fail: a
 name that fits two branches ends with status 0; a pin that does not resolve
 raises the error of a missing key; a clone with no seat's branch passes; and
 the sentence counts nothing it did not read. Tested against planted errors, 4
 of 4; computed once. 0 of 19.

